"""Smallest value. Accepts either multiple arguments (`min(3, 1, 2)` → 1) or a single iterable (`min([3, 1, 2])` → 1). Optional `key=fn` computes a comparison key per item — `min(words, key=lambda w: w.length)` returns the shortest word. Optional `default=v` (single-iterable form only) returns `v` when the input is empty instead of raising. Without `default=`, empty input raises. All compared values must be **comparable to each other** — all numbers, all strings, or all booleans. `key=` callbacks must be **pure** (no `wait`, `sleep`, `mine`, or any yielding action)."""
def min(a: Any, b: Any, *args: Any) -> float: ...
